==Battleground==
*1 [[Mr. Mer]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*4 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Henry]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Mr. Mer]] spawns.
**3 [[Mr. Mer]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns.
**6 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because of the sheer quantity of Traitless threats present, traditional meatshielding only gets so far when R.Ost shreds anything he didn't manage to finish. If that wasn't enough to deny disposable attackers and lower-ranged Wave Shields, Henry can Freeze large clusters of units at once, leaving them vulnerable to enemy frontliners. Upgrading the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] Style to reduce Henry's Freeze Uptime is helpful, but not necessary.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - A disposable LD unit with [[Massive Damage]] to Traitless, Wave and Freeze Immunity as well as enough range to evade the main pushers, a group of well-protected Hitmen can rain carnage and completely turn the game around. Just beware of its fragility and high speed, as meatshields may have difficulty catching up.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] - A rare case where its low range is less of an issue, Teacher BearCat deals [[Insane Damage]] to Traitless, offering a cheap yet powerful answer for Celeboodle, and can tank at least one Mini-Wave to rip huge chunks off Mr. Mer.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] - A midrange Anti-Traitless specialist, Jagando has a 100% chance to cause [[Knockback]] on his third hit, which helps to recover ground as Mr. Mer has only one knockback. Being [[Strong Against]] them with a level 1 [[Surge Attack]] on the same hit, Jagando can control entire clusters of traitless threats, all while dealing decent damage to them. Just make sure he doesn't get Frozen by Henry on the way.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] - Dancer, with all stat talents as well as [[Wave Attack|Wave]] and [[Freeze]] Immunity unlocked, becomes an excellent midranger who can deliver a quick burst of damage and also accumulate DPS.
*[[Lifeguard Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Lifeguard Cats]] - Despite their relatively low stats, they have the invaluable ability to slow traitless enemies whilst being immune to waves. By stacking them on the first Mr. Mer, you can keep the entire enemy field stuck in place while your other units pile on the damage.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - Having extreme health and high speed, Stone can pin the traitless pushers in place during its brief lifetime.
'''Recommended Ubers'''

* [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] - His LD anti-traitless nukes tear this stage to shreds, so long as he avoids [[Henry]]'s freeze which is easy enough to do thanks to his speed.

